Sweden has a history of strong political involvement by ordinary péople through its "popular movements" ("Folkrörelser" in Swedish), the most notable being &lt;a href="trade%20unions"&gt;trade unions&lt;/a&gt;, the &lt;a href="women%27s%20movement"&gt;women's movement&lt;/a&gt;, the &lt;a href="temperance%20movement"&gt;temperance movement&lt;/a&gt;, and - more recently - the sports movement. Election turnout in Sweden has always been high in international comparisons, although it has declined in recent decades, and is currently around 80% (80.11 in &lt;a href="Sweden%20general%20election%2C%202002"&gt;Sweden general election, 2002&lt;/a&gt;, 81.99 in &lt;a href="Sweden%20general%20election%2C%202006"&gt;Sweden general election, 2006&lt;/a&gt;).
